# Root build-context guard.
#
# The frontend image builds with the repository root as its context
# (`context: .` in .github/workflows/ci.yml), and Docker only reads a
# .dockerignore from the context root — the frontend/.dockerignore is
# therefore not applied to that build. This file is the only place that
# can keep developer- and CI-present env files (and heavy local build
# artifacts) out of the context-'.' image build. The per-directory
# .dockerignore files still govern their own contexts (backend/,
# frontend/ for local compose builds).
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
